// ?privateFireWeapon@Weapon@@QAE_NPBVObject@@PBUCoord3D@@0H1HHHPAH@Z
// partial score=0.1437 date=2026-09-29
// cl: /DNDEBUG /MD /O2 /Ob2 /GX-
// Open-BFME5: Weapon::privateFireWeapon, retail 0x001E9FD0 size 1253.
// Identity proven by ILT 0x00030A8A (?privateFireWeapon nine-arg) and ten
// matched callers. Frame matches retail (sub esp,0x20).
//
// Probe: ours 1138 vs retail 1253, 843 non-reloc diffs (was 850), 21 reloc
// drifts, first at +3.
//
// This session changed two things and measured both.
//
// 1. The linear-aim helper's "compiler-private ABI" is NOT private. Verdict #3
//    and the earlier banked header both recorded that ECX/EAX/EDI/ESI with no
//    stack arguments is unreachable from C++. It is reachable: a static
//    function with one call site and a body the inliner declines to expand
//    gets its four arguments in registers, and the register each pointer gets
//    follows the order the body first needs it. Reproducer, controls and the
//    ten-instruction prefix match are in
//    targets/game/reverse/identity_evidence/0x001e49e0-register-abi.md.
//    Including the helper's real body (sin/cos rotation of the step offset,
//    position.x added, terrain height through the virtual) in this TU, with a
//    large local to suppress inlining, turns the linear arm's call site into a
//    genuine out-of-line call. This is the whole 850 -> 843 gain and the
//    1140 -> 1138 size change.
//
// 2. RETAINED AS A FINDING, NOT APPLIED: the argument slot map is wrong in
//    this reconstruction and in game/.../Weapon_privateFireWeapon.cpp. Retail's
//    entry ESP disassembly puts the detonation test at +0x189 reading
//    [esp+0x4c] with ESP=E-0x30, i.e. E+0x1c = arg7, and the dispatch's ninth
//    argument at +0x21c reading [esp+0x48] = E+0x18 = arg6. So arg6 is a flags
//    word and arg7 is the detonation flag. Both this file and the game/ file
//    name arg6 isDetonation, and this file also names arg7 ignoreRanges.
//    Swapping the two names measured 1164 bytes / 884 diffs, worse than
//    leaving them, so the swap is NOT applied here; the caller-side naming in
//    Weapon_privateFireWeaponWrappers.cpp passes 1,1 in the two positions
//    (rva001EA5F0 and forceFireWeapon) and cannot yet separate them either.
//    Recorded, not shipped: see the re_log evidence line.
//
// Init-list WeaponBonus ctor tried: worse (1164B/1017 diffs). Victim-copy
// (targ) tried: 1134B/851, no gain. In-place scatterOffset multiply
// (off.x *= scalar) tried: 1148B/863, worse than the compound expression.
// Coord3D-local scatter form tried: 128B helper but breaks the register ABI
// (source arrives in edx, not edi).
//
// Remaining blockers, both global register allocation rather than statement
// order: (a) the prolog schedule -- retail loads extra->edx and source->ebx
// before eax=1.0f and interleaves the six bonus stores with the pushes, while
// this build stores the bonus first and keeps `this` in esi where retail keeps
// it in ebp (retail: this=ebp, victim=esi, delay=edi); (b) the 115-byte size
// shortfall downstream, which follows from (a) rather than from a missing
// statement. Declaration order alone does not move either.
#include <math.h>

